# representation — FAIRmat taxonomy module

Describes **in which form** the data of a material property is represented:
a scalar, a 1-D profile, an image or a volume. Built on the W3C RDF Data Cube
pattern (`qb:`) and QUDT units. All rules are OWL 2 axioms; a reasoner such as
HermiT reports a violation as an *unsatisfiable class* (TBox) or an
*inconsistent ontology* (ABox).

```text
tax:<MaterialProperty class>
  └─ rep:HasRepresentation ─▶ rep:<Type>
       └─ qb:structure ─▶ rep:DataStructureDefinition
            └─ qb:component ─▶ qb:ComponentSpecification
                 ├─ qb:dimension ─▶ rep:<Axis>     (+ rep:HasUnit <unit>, optional)
                 └─ qb:measure   ─▶ rep:<Signal>   (+ rep:HasUnit <unit>, optional)
```

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `representation.ttl` | the module (standalone) |
| `main.ttl` | FAIRmat taxonomy with the module appended |
| `TOOL_README.md` | GUI and reasoner usage |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | all changes and test results |

| Prefix | Namespace |
|---|---|
| `rep:` | `http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/representation#` |
| `tax:` | `http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/` |
| `qb:` | `http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#` |
| `qudt:` | `http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/` |
| `unit:` | `http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/` |
| `qk:` | `http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/` |

---

## 1. Axioms

**Strict** = enforced by the reasoner. **Canonical** = shipped vocabulary or
intended use; extendable (see §4).

### 1.1 Representation types

| Type | Parent | Rank | Max. dimensions | Axis | Measures |
|---|---|---:|---:|---|---|
| `rep:Scalar` | Representation | 0 | 0 | none | any Signal |
| `rep:Profile` | Representation | 1 | 1 | any Axis | any Signal |
| `rep:Spectrum` | Profile | 1 | 1 | any Axis (canonical: `Energy`) | any Signal |
| `rep:TimeSeries` | Profile | 1 | 1 | **`Time` only** | any Signal |
| `rep:DepthProfile` | Profile | 1 | 1 | any Axis (canonical: `Depth`) | any Signal |
| `rep:Image` | Representation | 2 | 2 | any Axis (canonical: `X`, `Y`) | any Signal |
| `rep:VolumeData` | Representation | 3 | 3 | any Axis (canonical: `X`, `Y`, `Z`) | any Signal |

All rank rules are strict: a representation has exactly one rank; a type is
*defined* by its rank (rank 0 ⇔ Scalar, …); types of different rank exclude
each other; every type is also a `qb:DataSet`.

### 1.2 Scalar

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| rank 0 | strict |
| its DSD has measure components only — no dimension | strict |

### 1.3 Profile

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| rank 1 | strict |
| at most 1 dimension | strict |

### 1.4 Spectrum

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| a Profile: rank 1, at most 1 dimension | strict |
| energy axis (`rep:Energy`) | canonical |

### 1.5 TimeSeries

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| a Profile: rank 1, at most 1 dimension | strict |
| the only permitted axis is `rep:Time` | strict |

### 1.6 DepthProfile

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| a Profile: rank 1, at most 1 dimension | strict |
| depth axis (`rep:Depth`) | canonical |

### 1.7 Image

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| rank 2, at most 2 dimensions | strict |
| axes `rep:X`, `rep:Y` | canonical |

### 1.8 VolumeData

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| rank 3, at most 3 dimensions | strict |
| axes `rep:X`, `rep:Y`, `rep:Z` | canonical |

### 1.9 Structure (DSD and component specifications)

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| a `qb:dimension` must be an Axis, a `qb:measure` must be a Signal | strict |
| one dimension per component specification | strict |
| `rep:DataStructureDefinition` is a `qb:DataStructureDefinition` | strict |

### 1.10 Components

| Component | Kind | Quantity kind | Canonical unit |
|---|---|---|---|
| `rep:X`, `rep:Y`, `rep:Z` | Axis | `qk:Length` | `unit:MicroM` |
| `rep:Depth` | Axis | `qk:Length` | `unit:NanoM` |
| `rep:Energy` | Axis | `qk:Energy` | `unit:EV` |
| `rep:Time` | Axis | `qk:Time` | `unit:SEC` |
| `rep:Intensity` | Signal | `tax:Intensity` | `unit:COUNT` |
| `rep:Temperature` | Signal | `qk:Temperature` | `unit:K` |

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| a component is exactly one of Axis / Signal / UnitAttribute | strict |
| Axis / Signal / UnitAttribute are `qb:` dimension / measure / attribute properties | strict |
| at most one quantity kind per component | strict |
| the listed components are different individuals | strict |
| the list of components, their quantity kinds and canonical units | canonical |

### 1.11 Units

| Quantity kind | Permitted units |
|---|---|
| `qk:Temperature` | `unit:K` |
| `qk:Length` | `unit:NanoM`, `unit:MicroM` |
| `qk:Time` | `unit:SEC` |
| `qk:Energy` | `unit:EV` |
| `tax:Intensity` | `unit:COUNT` |

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| a unit is optional; at most one per component or specification | strict |
| the unit must be permitted for the quantity kind (table above), on the component itself or on a spec through its dimension / measure | strict |
| the listed units are different individuals | strict |
| a quantity kind can never be used as a unit | strict |
| the permitted-unit table and the list of units | canonical |

### 1.12 Taxonomy link

| Rule | Kind |
|---|---|
| `rep:HasRepresentation`: from a `tax:MaterialProperty` to a `rep:Representation`, at most one | strict |
| `rep:HasDataStructureDefinition`: from a `tax:MaterialProperty` to a DSD, at most one | strict |
| hence a class (and its subclasses) cannot get representations of different rank | strict |

---

## 2. Usage at TBox level (taxonomy classes)

A taxonomy class gets **one nested restriction** (`rdfs:subClassOf`).
One `qb:component` block per axis and per signal; units go on the
specification. Manchester syntax below; the GUI (`TOOL_README.md`) produces the
same as Turtle. All examples are consistent with `main.ttl`.

### 2.1 Scalar

```text
tax:MeltingTemperature SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:Scalar
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Temperature) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:K))))))
```

### 2.2 Profile

```text
tax:ElementalComposition SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:Profile
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:X) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:MicroM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Intensity) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:COUNT))))))
```

### 2.3 Spectrum

```text
tax:ElectronicDensityOfStates SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:Spectrum
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:Energy) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:EV)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Intensity) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:COUNT))))))
```

### 2.4 TimeSeries

```text
tax:CarrierLifetime SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:TimeSeries
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:Time) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:SEC)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Intensity) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:COUNT))))))
```

### 2.5 DepthProfile

```text
tax:LayerThickness SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:DepthProfile
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:Depth) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:NanoM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Intensity) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:COUNT))))))
```

### 2.6 Image

```text
tax:GrainSize SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:Image
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:Y) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:MicroM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:X) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:MicroM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Intensity) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:COUNT))))))
```

### 2.7 VolumeData

```text
tax:Porosity SubClassOf rep:HasRepresentation some (rep:VolumeData
  and (qb:structure some (rep:DataStructureDefinition
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:Z) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:MicroM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:Y) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:MicroM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:dimension value rep:X) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:MicroM)))
    and (qb:component some (qb:ComponentSpecification
          and (qb:measure value rep:Intensity) and (rep:HasUnit value unit:COUNT))))))
```

**Mistakes the reasoner rejects** (the class becomes unsatisfiable): a Scalar with
a dimension; a TimeSeries axis other than `Time`; more dimensions than the rank;
an Axis as measure or a Signal as dimension; a unit not permitted for the
quantity kind; a class and its superclass with representations of different rank.

---

## 3. Usage at ABox level (instance data)

Named individuals for the sample, its dataset, the DSD, one specification per
component, and observations. The type of the dataset gives the rank
(`rep:Rank` may be stated; it must agree). Component IRIs are used as data
properties on observations. All examples are consistent with `main.ttl`.

Common prefixes:

```turtle
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/data/> .
@prefix rep:  <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/representation#> .
@prefix tax:  <http://fairmat-nfdi.eu/taxonomy/> .
@prefix qb:   <http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
```

### 3.1 Scalar

```turtle
ex:mp-1 a tax:MeltingTemperature ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:mp-1-data .
ex:mp-1-data a rep:Scalar ; qb:structure ex:mp-1-dsd .
ex:mp-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:mp-1-t .
ex:mp-1-t a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Temperature ; rep:HasUnit unit:K .
ex:mp-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:mp-1-data ; rep:Temperature "1357.77"^^xsd:double .
```

### 3.2 Profile

```turtle
ex:ec-1 a tax:ElementalComposition ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:ec-1-data .
ex:ec-1-data a rep:Profile ; qb:structure ex:ec-1-dsd .
ex:ec-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:ec-1-x , ex:ec-1-i .
ex:ec-1-x a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:X ; rep:HasUnit unit:MicroM .
ex:ec-1-i a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Intensity ; rep:HasUnit unit:COUNT .
ex:ec-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:ec-1-data ;
    rep:X "0.5"^^xsd:double ; rep:Intensity "812"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
```

### 3.3 Spectrum

```turtle
ex:dos-1 a tax:ElectronicDensityOfStates ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:dos-1-data .
ex:dos-1-data a rep:Spectrum ; qb:structure ex:dos-1-dsd .
ex:dos-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:dos-1-e , ex:dos-1-i .
ex:dos-1-e a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:Energy ; rep:HasUnit unit:EV .
ex:dos-1-i a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Intensity ; rep:HasUnit unit:COUNT .
ex:dos-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:dos-1-data ;
    rep:Energy "10.5"^^xsd:double ; rep:Intensity "142"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
```

### 3.4 TimeSeries

```turtle
ex:cl-1 a tax:CarrierLifetime ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:cl-1-data .
ex:cl-1-data a rep:TimeSeries ; qb:structure ex:cl-1-dsd .
ex:cl-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:cl-1-t , ex:cl-1-i .
ex:cl-1-t a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:Time ; rep:HasUnit unit:SEC .
ex:cl-1-i a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Intensity ; rep:HasUnit unit:COUNT .
ex:cl-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:cl-1-data ;
    rep:Time "1.0e-9"^^xsd:double ; rep:Intensity "101"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
```

### 3.5 DepthProfile

```turtle
ex:lt-1 a tax:LayerThickness ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:lt-1-data .
ex:lt-1-data a rep:DepthProfile ; qb:structure ex:lt-1-dsd .
ex:lt-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:lt-1-d , ex:lt-1-i .
ex:lt-1-d a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:Depth ; rep:HasUnit unit:NanoM .
ex:lt-1-i a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Intensity ; rep:HasUnit unit:COUNT .
ex:lt-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:lt-1-data ;
    rep:Depth "25.0"^^xsd:double ; rep:Intensity "125"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
```

### 3.6 Image

```turtle
ex:gs-1 a tax:GrainSize ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:gs-1-data .
ex:gs-1-data a rep:Image ; qb:structure ex:gs-1-dsd .
ex:gs-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:gs-1-y , ex:gs-1-x , ex:gs-1-i .
ex:gs-1-y a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:Y ; rep:HasUnit unit:MicroM .
ex:gs-1-x a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:X ; rep:HasUnit unit:MicroM .
ex:gs-1-i a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Intensity ; rep:HasUnit unit:COUNT .
ex:gs-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:gs-1-data ;
    rep:Y "0"^^xsd:double ; rep:X "1"^^xsd:double ; rep:Intensity "140"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
```

### 3.7 VolumeData

```turtle
ex:po-1 a tax:Porosity ; rep:HasRepresentation ex:po-1-data .
ex:po-1-data a rep:VolumeData ; qb:structure ex:po-1-dsd .
ex:po-1-dsd a rep:DataStructureDefinition ; qb:component ex:po-1-z , ex:po-1-y , ex:po-1-x , ex:po-1-i .
ex:po-1-z a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:Z ; rep:HasUnit unit:MicroM .
ex:po-1-y a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:Y ; rep:HasUnit unit:MicroM .
ex:po-1-x a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:dimension rep:X ; rep:HasUnit unit:MicroM .
ex:po-1-i a qb:ComponentSpecification ; qb:measure rep:Intensity ; rep:HasUnit unit:COUNT .
ex:po-1-obs a rep:Observation ; qb:dataSet ex:po-1-data ;
    rep:Z "0"^^xsd:double ; rep:Y "1"^^xsd:double ; rep:X "1"^^xsd:double ;
    rep:Intensity "147"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
```

**Mistakes the reasoner rejects** (the ontology becomes inconsistent): a unit not
permitted for the quantity kind; two units on one specification; an Axis as
measure; more dimension specifications than the rank; a TimeSeries with an axis
other than `Time`; a Scalar with a dimension or a stated rank ≠ 0; a sample with
two representations of different rank.

---

## 4. Mathematics (description logic)

Abbreviations: `str` = `qb:structure`, `comp` = `qb:component`, `dim` = `qb:dimension`,
`meas` = `qb:measure`, `HR` = `HasRepresentation`, `HQK` = `HasQuantityKind`,
`HU` = `HasUnit`, `DSD` = `rep:DataStructureDefinition`.

### 4.1 Strict axioms

**Rank and types**

```text
Scalar     ≡ Representation ⊓ ∃Rank.{0}          Spectrum     ⊑ Profile
Profile    ≡ Representation ⊓ ∃Rank.{1}          TimeSeries   ⊑ Profile
Image      ≡ Representation ⊓ ∃Rank.{2}          DepthProfile ⊑ Profile
VolumeData ≡ Representation ⊓ ∃Rank.{3}          Scalar, Profile, Image, VolumeData ⊑ qb:DataSet
Func(Rank)
```

**Type rules**

```text
Scalar     ⊑ ∀str.∀comp.(∃meas.⊤ ⊓ ¬∃dim.⊤)            measures only
TimeSeries ⊑ ∀str.∀comp.∀dim.{Time}                     axis is Time
Profile    ⊑ ∀str.(≤1 comp.∃dim.⊤)                      rank limit 1
Image      ⊑ ∀str.(≤2 comp.∃dim.⊤)                      rank limit 2
VolumeData ⊑ ∀str.(≤3 comp.∃dim.⊤)                      rank limit 3
```

**Structure**

```text
DSD ⊑ Representation ⊓ qb:DataStructureDefinition
DSD ⊑ ∀comp.(∀dim.Axis ⊓ ∀meas.Signal)                  strict roles
DSD ⊑ ∀comp.(≤1 dim.⊤)                                  one dimension per spec
```

**Components**

```text
ComponentProperty ≡ Axis ⊔ Signal ⊔ UnitAttribute,  pairwise disjoint
Axis ⊑ qb:DimensionProperty    Signal ⊑ qb:MeasureProperty    UnitAttribute ⊑ qb:AttributeProperty
Func(HQK)     ∃HQK.⊤ ⊑ ComponentProperty     ⊤ ⊑ ∀HQK.qudt:QuantityKind
X, Y, Z, Depth, Energy, Time, Intensity, Temperature   pairwise different
```

**Units**

```text
Func(HU)      ∃HU.⊤ ⊑ ComponentProperty ⊔ qb:ComponentSpecification      ⊤ ⊑ ∀HU.qudt:Unit
qudt:Unit ⊓ qudt:QuantityKind ⊑ ⊥
EV, K, MicroM, NanoM, SEC, COUNT   pairwise different

for each quantity kind k with permitted units U(k):
  ∃HQK.{k} ⊔ ∃dim.∃HQK.{k} ⊔ ∃meas.∃HQK.{k}  ⊑  ∀HU.U(k)

  U(Temperature) = {K}      U(Length) = {NanoM, MicroM}      U(Time) = {SEC}
  U(Energy)      = {EV}     U(Intensity) = {COUNT}
```

**Taxonomy link**

```text
Func(HR)    ∃HR.⊤ ⊑ tax:MaterialProperty    ⊤ ⊑ ∀HR.Representation
Func(HasDataStructureDefinition)    ∃HasDataStructureDefinition.⊤ ⊑ tax:MaterialProperty
⊤ ⊑ ∀HasDataStructureDefinition.DSD
```

### 4.2 Canonical assertions

```text
Axis(X)  Axis(Y)  Axis(Z)  Axis(Depth)  Axis(Energy)  Axis(Time)      Signal(Intensity)  Signal(Temperature)
HQK(X, Length)   HQK(Y, Length)   HQK(Z, Length)   HQK(Depth, Length)
HQK(Energy, Energy)   HQK(Time, Time)   HQK(Intensity, tax:Intensity)   HQK(Temperature, Temperature)
HU(X, MicroM)    HU(Y, MicroM)    HU(Z, MicroM)    HU(Depth, NanoM)
HU(Energy, EV)   HU(Time, SEC)    HU(Intensity, COUNT)   HU(Temperature, K)
```

Intended (not axioms): Spectrum → `Energy`, DepthProfile → `Depth`,
Image → `X`, `Y`, VolumeData → `X`, `Y`, `Z`.

### 4.3 Extending the canonical vocabulary

The strict axioms are general; the canonical vocabulary is a starting set.

| To add | From | Add | Effect |
|---|---|---|---|
| a component | the taxonomy (`tax:`) or an external vocabulary | `Axis(c)` or `Signal(c)`, `HQK(c, k)`, optionally `HU(c, u)`; add `c` to the pairwise-different components | all strict rules apply to `c` (roles, rank limits, TimeSeries, unit table) |
| a unit | QUDT (`unit:`) or an external vocabulary | `qudt:Unit(u)`; add `u` to the pairwise-different units and to `U(k)` of its quantity kind | `u` becomes permitted for `k` |
| a quantity kind | QUDT (`qk:`), the taxonomy, or external | `qudt:QuantityKind(k)` and one unit axiom `… ⊑ ∀HU.U(k)` | units for `k` are checked |
| an intended axis made strict | — | copy the TimeSeries rule: `T ⊑ ∀str.∀comp.∀dim.{a₁, …}` | other axes are rejected for `T` |

Terms used without these declarations (e.g. an external component typed
nowhere) are accepted: the reasoner infers them to be an Axis or a Signal from
the slot they are in, and does not count or reject them unless they are
declared different from the listed ones.